name        = "Bleu's Improved Tooltips"
source_dir  = "source"
output_dir  = "output"
description = [=[[b]Puts the numbers a commander actually needs into the commander tooltips.[/b] Research times, ability cooldowns, and structure health and armour, on the tooltip you are already looking at - no alt-tabbing to a wiki mid-round.

[h1]What it adds[/h1]

[list]
[*] [b]Research time[/b] - an hourglass and a number on every research and upgrade. Armour 3 reads "40 res, 120 seconds" instead of just "40 res".
[*] [b]Cooldown[/b] - a stopwatch on commander abilities: Bone Wall, Power Surge, Nutrient Mist, Rupture, Heal Wave, Cyst, and the rest.
[*] [b]Health and armour[/b] - shown under the description for anything you drop or build, on both teams.
[/list]

[h1]Live values[/h1]

Numbers that change during a round are read live rather than printed from a table. Bone Wall's health scales with your biomass level, so at Biomass 9 the tooltip says 900, not 100.

[h1]Works with other mods[/h1]

Nothing is hardcoded per tech. The mod reads the same tech data the game itself uses to make a tech function, so tech added by other mods gets improved tooltips automatically, with no patch needed here. Modders can register their own value resolvers for anything they compute at runtime - see the README on GitHub.

[h1]Client side only[/h1]

Every value is already available on your own machine, so the server does not need to run this mod. Subscribe and it works anywhere.

Source: https://github.com/Bleuitup/Bleus-Improved-Tooltips]=]
image       = "preview.jpg"
